    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Jor’maelis is centered at -46.374220, 130.627031 under Communalism, with 105,431,000 people across 13 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Jor’maelis occupies 10,194,632.18 sq mi / 26,403,976.13 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 5.176582% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Underwater without reefs, Beach and grass with water and Partial forest define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Ocean Surface floating settlement, Beach and grass with water, Underwater without reefs, Partial forest and Farming. Population density is 3.993 people/sq km / 10.342 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Elemental and Energy-Born Peoples, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Triton, Merfolk, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi, Hadozee, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Nefaric Veil, with worship and patronage records naming Nefarokir, Eirzunet, Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Iskareth, Sigrananna, Bastveig, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 6 recorded four-province geography group links, including 5 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
