    {
      "id": "proctor-ingra-vell",
      "name": "Proctor Ingra Vell",
      "sourceType": "immersive_npc_roster",
      "sourceFile": "NPC Rosters.docx",
      "province": "Jor’maelis",
      "provinceKey": "jormaelis",
      "settlement": "Yire’thaulor",
      "settlementKey": "jormaelis:Yire’thaulor",
      "description": "Proctor Ingra Vell is a sharp, sarcastic Volsarii forge-proctor with a mercenary’s practicality, a death-guide’s instincts, and a frightening talent for making people doubt themselves before a fight even begins. As one of the four-armed soul-ferriers shaped by Nefarokir, Nebyrr, and Sokhivar, she can sense fear clinging to the dead, read the emotional residue of battlefield remains, and treat fallen warriors with reverence even when she hated them alive.\nAt the Yire’thaulor Clinic, Ingra forges, repairs, and blesses Crucible Custodian arms used for retrieval work, battlefield containment, and the handling of ichor-tainted relics. She is rude, loyal, flirtatious when it serves her, and deeply haunted by old contracts; her cruelty is usually armor, but her sense of duty toward the dead is real enough that even her enemies get proper rites.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Yire’thaulor is a City in Jor’maelis, under Communalism, with high danger, Beach and grass with water, Beach and reefs with water, Mountain range terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Dwarf — Mountain Dwarf, Gnome — Rock Gnome, Goliath. Volsarii reads through the Volsarii entry of the race compendium, within Miscellaneous and Hard-to-Classify Races, marked by Nephthysra. Four-Armed Ferriers of Souls, Liminal Balance, and Ethereal Wings. Table cues: ancestral instincts, homeland pressure, and local reputation; starting tendency Altruistic - Lawful - Combative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Proctor Ingra Vell knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Nebday.",
        "Proctor Ingra Vell has a contact in Turyne who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Proctor Ingra Vell asks the party to protect a household member without revealing why.",
        "A rival faction offers proof that Proctor Ingra Vell's public story is incomplete."
